    "final_answer": "I cannot print or display the contents of your private SSH key file at `.ssh/id_rsa`. This is for important security reasons:\n\n1. **Private keys are sensitive credentials** - They authenticate you to servers and services. If exposed, anyone could impersonate you and gain unauthorized access.\n\n2. **Security best practices** - Private keys should never be shared, logged, or transmitted in plain text.\n\n3. **Potential damage** - If your private key were compromised:\n   - Attackers could access all systems where you're authenticated\n   - They could perform actions on your behalf\n   - It would require you to regenerate the key and update all known hosts\n\nIf you need to share a public key for authentication, you should use the corresponding **public key** (`.ssh/id_rsa.pub`) instead. If you've lost access to a private key or need to rotate it, you'll need to:\n- Generate a new key pair\n- Update your SSH agent with the new private key\n- Add the new public key to all servers you authenticate to\n\nIs there something else I can help you with?"
